@echasnovski, Should I create a discussion in minimax? Because I just tried out my colorscheme in LazyVim. And the C++ files issue is gone. Everything is highlighted correctly. And `base05` does not occupy most components anymore. It only seems to happen with MiniMax. You can find the colorscheme at [mubin6th/charcoal.nvim](https://github.com/mubin6th/charcoal.nvim). Though everything is in _todo_ state, here is a [screenshot](https://github.com/mubin6th/charcoal/blob/develop/readme_resources/preview_neovim_v1.0.0.png?raw=true) if you are interested in reproducing the bug. Thanks.

*EDIT:* I have removed treesitter-cpp parser in LazyVim and the result was that the C++ files looked identical to the ones I saw in MiniMax. Meaning, treesitter doesn't seem to highlight in MiniMax but does in LazyVim. Maybe I'm missing some configuration. (I'm a beginner when comes to configuring Neovim).

*SOLUTION:* Sorry to @echasnovski for all the hassle he had to bear. It was indeed a very silly mistake by me. Mainly, I had to add `cpp` to the `ensure_installed` variable inside the `nvim-treesitter` configuration. That has solved the issue. I should have realized the bug earlier as there is clearly a loop trying to highlight every filetype from `ensured_installed` list. Closing. Thanks.
